# OS/7 base system — installed on EVERY architecture, in every mode.
#
# The two architectures are different products:
#   amd64 - GUI or headless, chosen at install time. Adds the desktop from
#           package-lists-amd64/ and the Microsoft GUI stack from hooks-amd64/.
#   arm64 - SERVER ONLY. No GUI target, so no desktop list. os7-setup is
#           text-mode, so it installs this architecture too.
#
# README's "one shared package base" is per-architecture, so this split is
# consistent with it. Everything below is common to both.
#
# IMPORTANT: live-build package lists do NOT support trailing inline comments.
# Every token on a non-comment line is passed to apt as a package name.
# Keep comments on their own lines. (docs/BUILD-NOTES.md #9)

ubuntu-standard

# casper provides the Ubuntu live-boot init. live-build's ubuntu mode pulls it
# in by default, but naming it explicitly keeps the ISO's live-bootability from
# depending on a default. (docs/BUILD-NOTES.md #5)
casper

# --- Storage: ZFS root -------------------------------------------------------
# The GA-kernel-matched PREBUILT module, never zfs-dkms, so kernel and ZFS move
# in lockstep. Validated 2026-08-22: docs/SESSION-0-ZFS-VALIDATION.md
zfsutils-linux
zfs-initramfs

# linux-generic carries the matching prebuilt zfs.ko. Do NOT swap this for a
# -virtual or -kvm flavour: those do not ship the ZFS module.
linux-generic

# --- Identity: Entra ID login ------------------------------------------------
# authd is in the archive. Its Entra broker (authd-msentraid) is NOT - it is a
# Canonical snap, and seeding snaps into a live-build image is unsolved here.
# See installer/README.md.
authd

# --- .NET (README: Core, non-negotiable, both modes) --------------------------
# resolute ships .NET 10, not 9. Canonical packages this now; it does not come
# from packages.microsoft.com any more.
dotnet-sdk-10.0

# --- Base tooling ------------------------------------------------------------
openssh-server
curl
ca-certificates
gnupg
sudo
git
less
vim
